-- title:
--   Hecke stability of the toric points of the Néron object
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a non-zero level $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $p$ in the sense that $p$ belongs to $A$'s set of non-units, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Let $\Lambda$ be a level datum for $(p,M,H)$ over $A$: a section $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \mathrm{base}\,p$ compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ with a morphism $f$ to $\mathrm{base}\,p$ carrying a relative group law over $\mathrm{baseRing}\,p$, together with identifications of $J_H(M/p)$ with the generic-fibre points of $f$ and of the degree-zero divisor class group of the function field over the residue field of $A$ with the points over $\mathrm{resPt}\,A$ followed by $\sigma_A$. Assume $\Lambda.f$ satisfies the abelian-scheme property bundle: it is smooth and proper, its fibres are connected, and it admits a relative group law. Let $O$ be a Néron object for $J_H(M)$ at $p$ over $\Lambda$, so in particular a scheme $G$ smooth, separated, locally of finite type, quasi-compact and surjective over $\mathrm{base}\,p$ with preconnected fibres, a commutative relative group law, an additive and Galois-equivariant identification $\mathrm{pts}$ of $J_H(M)$ with the generic-fibre points, and for each set $S$ of naturals and each generator $t \in \mathrm{CohCarrier.Gen}\,M\,S$ an endomorphism $\mathrm{hecke}\,S\,t$ of $G$ over the base that is additive for the group law and induces $\mathrm{genOpH}\,M\,H\,S\,t$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points. Then for every $m > 0$, every generator $g$ of $\mathrm{CohCarrier.Gen}\,M\,S$ (that is, $T_\ell$ for a prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid M$, $U_q$ for a prime $q \mid M$, or a diamond $\langle d \rangle$ for $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$) and every $x \in J_H(M)$ lying in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$, the subgroup of $J_H(M)$ generated by the range of $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m$, the element $\mathrm{genOpH}\,M\,H\,S\,g\,x$ again lies in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$.
--
--   This is the stability of the toric part of the Néron model at $p$ under the Hecke operators, in the form needed for the $m$-torsion points of the torus: the subgroup $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$ is a module over the Hecke generators. It feeds the analysis of the toric filtration of the Tate module and the computation of the action of $U_p$ on toric points by the cyclotomic character, used in turn in the level-lowering step at $p$.
